      "title": "Andy Burnham faces climate revolt after approval of North Sea gas drilling",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/20/jackdaw-north-sea-gas-field-to-get-go-ahead-in-blow-to-climate-campaigners",
      "description": "<p>Jackdaw gasfield announcement signals UK’s commitment to North Sea industry but undermines green credentials</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/20/what-does-the-approval-of-the-jackdaw-gasfield-mean\">What does the approval of the Jackdaw gasfield mean?</a></p></li></ul><p>The Jackdaw gasfield will be given the go-ahead on Wednesday, signalling Andy Burnham’s commitment to the North Sea fossil fuel industry and threatening to trigger a row with climate campaigners and Labour MPs.</p><p>Miatta Fahnbulleh and John Healey, the energy secretary and chancellor respectively, will make the announcement from Aberdeen on Wednesday morning after more than a year of deliberations over whether doing so would violate the UK’s climate commitments.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/20/jackdaw-north-sea-gas-field-to-get-go-ahead-in-blow-to-climate-campaigners\">Continue reading...</a>",
